        "node_id": "n_2_e8ac3e",
        "thought_text": "The issue lies in the double counting of numbers that contain the power of 2 as a substring. The dynamic programming approach is unnecessarily complex and prone to errors. A simpler approach would be to iterate through each number from 0 to n, convert it to a string, and check if the substring representation of \\(2^e\\) is present. This direct method avoids the pitfalls of dynamic programming and ensures accurate counting.",
